 "answer": "Run this in each database that has the extension:\n\n```sql\nALTER EXTENSION vector UPDATE;\n```\n\nTo upgrade to a specific version instead of the default, use `ALTER EXTENSION vector UPDATE TO '<version>';`.\n\nTo check the installed version before and after, run:\n\n```sql\nSELECT extversion FROM pg_extension WHERE extname = 'vector';\n```\n\nYou can list the versions the server can upgrade to with `SELECT * FROM pg_available_extension_versions WHERE name = 'vector';`.\n\nThe new binaries must be installed on the server first. Otherwise the upgrade has nothing new to load.",
